Dear Eugenio,
here is my proposal for organizing ACA 08 at RISC:

1.
RISC Summer 08
At this moment, the following conferences are already fixed as part of the "RISC Summer 08":

RTA 08 (Rewrite Techniques and Applications) July 14 - 18, 
Conference Chairman: Buchberger
ISSAC 08 (International Symposium on Symbolic and Algebraic 
Computation) July 20 - 23, Conference Chairman Winkler
SFB-SC 08 (Final Conference of the Special Research Area 
"Scientific Computing") July 25 - 27, Conference Chairman Paule
AB 08 (Algebraic Biology) Date not yet fixed, but should be 
collocated with the three conferences above, Conference Chairman 
Buchberger
(Other conferences or workshops may be added within the next few weeks)

2.
Synergies with other RISC conferences:

As I said in my previous mails, I think that ACA 08 would ideally 
fit into the family of these conferences with lots of interactions 
and synergies with ISSAC and AB but also with SFB-SC and RTA. 
Participants in any of these conferences might be highly motivated to 
also participate in ACA and vice versa. Thus, having ACA 08 at RISC, 
in my view, is a unique opportunity.

3.
Date of ACA 08: 
I see two alternatives:

a) RTA, ISSAC, ACA, AB, SFB-SC
b) RTA, ISSAC, SFB-SC, ACA, AB

I think that, scientifically, alternative a) is superior and 
actually ideal, because the participants of ISSAC may continue to 
stay for ACA and the participants of AB may be motivated to come 
earlier already for ACA and, of course the topic of AB is just a 
special topic of ACA and so ACA and AB may even overlap for at least 
one day. The problem with a) is that for realizing it, we would 
have to shift the dates of SFB-SC slightly. Unfortunately, Peter 
Paule (the chairman of SFB-SC) cannot be reached until August 15. 
Thus, I cannot guarantee at this moment whether this alternative can 
be realized. However, I know from his secretary that the dates of 
SFB-SC are not yet completely fixed and in my view I think it would 
be very beneficial also for SFB-SC to exploit the synergy with ACA 
and AB.

Alternative b) is still full of synergies and hence very attractive 
and can be easily realized because I have not yet fixed the date of 
AB.
My bid is based on the assumption that we fix alternative a) or b) 
at latest by August 18.

4.
Responsibilities:
Buchberger: initialization, overall coordination and ultimate 
responsibility, in particular ultimate financial responsibility.
Wolfgang Windsteiger: Co-chair and local chairman (Wolfgang 
Windsteiger is an experienced faculty and researcher in my theorema 
group and he did an excellent job as chairman of two conferences in 
the frame of the RISC Summer 2007, namely Calculemus and MKM; I would 
like to propose that he is named not only as local chair but also as 
