5.
Site: Castle of Hagenberg, home of RISC
In the past ten years we've hosted over 30 conferences at RISC. I 
think it is fair to say that participants always were excited about 
the particular flair of the place and also were always satisfied with 
the efficiency of our organization. Thus we guarantee professional 
organization at a unique research and conference site.
In the past two days we haven't had the time to set up an example of 
a homepage for ACA 08. However, please see the various websites of 
the 11 conferences we had in the course of RISC Summer 2007 
(www.risc.uni-linz.ac.at).

6.
Finances, Fees etc.:
Our experience shows that cost-covering conference fees are not 
only important for a sound financial basis but also very important 
psychologically:
Things that do not cost anything aren't worth anything. However, we 
will raise significant additional funds that will enable us to 
invite a couple of renowned keynote speakers and to provide a number 
of fellowships for qualified participants:
Details:
- 250 Euro conference fee for a three-day conference (including 
meals, coffee breaks, proceedings etc.)
- 50 Euro for conference dinner
- RISC covers the cost of three invited speakers.
- RISC provides fellowships for fees (excluding and including 
meals) for qualified researchers on the basis of applications and 
depending on available funds, at least 15 fellowships. Typical prerequisites for 
obtaining a fellowship: Presentation of a paper and proof of 
financial need. In some special cases we may also support travel costs.
All fund-raising will be done by RISC. However, any additional effort 
by the steering committee etc. is highly welcome.

7.
Marketing and announcements:
We assume that the main responsibility for efficient marketing and 
conference announcements etc. is with the program committee. 
However, of course, we will also feel strongly motivated and 
committed to announce the conference widely through our experienced 
RISC communication channels.
I do hope that, based on the unique synergies with the other 
conferences at RISC, the steering committee will let us organize 
also ACA 08 and I guarantee that we will put all our expertise and 
effort into this important event for making it the most successful 
ACA conference ever and laying a foundation for a new vigorous 
future of the important applications of computer algebra.
If you need any additional information, please let me know immediately.

